<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abd Allah Beg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abd <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allah">Allah</a> Beg was the leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hami">Kumul</a> (Hami) oasis in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinjiang">Xinjiang</a> who submitted to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kangxi-emperor">Kangxi Emperor</a> of the Qing in 1696, as the Dzungar Khanate threatened the region. He helped Qing armies against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungars">Dzungars</a> and was rewarded with a hereditary rank. His descendants ruled Hami as Qing-appointed princes (wang) into the 20th century.</p></div>
